{
  "_comment": "Model profiles. One entry = one model name that Claude Code, Continue and the scripts can ask for. 'role': agent (offered to the agent and by the installer), autocomplete (Continue), compare (benchmark only). 'file' is a GGUF file in the models folder; 'download' says where scripts\\Get-Model.ps1 gets it and the other files of the profile (Hugging Face repository, pinned revision, size, SHA-256), or names a profile with the same files. 'mmproj' in args is the image encoder of a model, also a file in the models folder. 'args' are llama-server options without the leading dashes (llama-server --help); 'defaults' apply to every profile. No GPU split and no device names here: llama.cpp fits each model to the cards it finds (--fit), values tuned for one machine belong in config\\machine.json. Paths in 'chat-template-file' are relative to config\\. After a change run scripts\\Restart-Server.ps1. Details: docs\\models.md.",
